<title>UK: Albright says phosphates demand still strong.</title>
<headline>Albright says phosphates demand still strong.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>British chemicals group Albright &amp; Wilson Plc said on Wednesday that phosphates demand remains strong in all its markets, although progress in Europe is being more than offset by the impact of the strength of sterling.</p>
<p>The group's speciality chemicals businesses continue to move forward in the Americas and Asia, but again are being held back in Europe by sterling's strength, chairman Sir Christopher Benson told the annual meeting.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
